title: Renaissance Steps 1–2 — the v7 task DAG goes web-reachable
summary: 'Built the data layer the Tasks UI will render. Step 1: added a claimant filter to TaskFilter + a tasksForClaimant() convenience in paradigm-mcp''s task-loader (the Task carried claimant but nothing could query on it) — the prerequisite for both the agent inbox and human swim-lanes, +5 tests. Step 2: a new read-only /api/tasks/* route (list w/ filters, /board lifting assembleCaptainBoard onto HTTP for the first time, /inbox per-claimant, /:id) + tasks as an always-on section. Smoke-tested live against the real store: board shows 13 open/11 unclaimed, human inbox returns 2 tasks, 400/404 guards correct. MCP 430 / CLI 441 green.'
