learnings:
  - The captain board (assembleCaptainBoard) was MCP/CLI-only — lifting it onto an HTTP route is what makes the v7 run-DAG visible to any web surface for the first time. Called without a ProjectContext it skips ripple scoring and stays fast (scores 0); the route trades ripple-rank for latency, which is right for a list render.
  - Cross-package imports from platform-server into paradigm-mcp use the proven '../../../../paradigm-mcp/src/...' relative path (mirrors symphony.ts/docs.ts) and tsup bundles them into the CLI dist — no separate build wiring needed.
  - The claimant filter needed kind-narrowing because refs collide across kinds (a human and an archetype can both be reffed 'forge') — ref-only match would cross-contaminate the agent inbox with human tasks.
